{
  "summary": "Increases the polling frequency in the Python functional test framework for node synchronization helpers and the RPC readiness wait loop. In sync_blocks and sync_mempools, the default sleep interval between checks drops from 1 second to 0.05 seconds, while wait_for_rpc_connection increases polling frequency from 4 to 20 times per second and switches to an absolute wall-clock timeout.",
  "problem": "Functional tests spend idle time waiting for conservative 1-second sleep intervals to elapse even when node state synchronization or RPC readiness completes in milliseconds, unnecessarily prolonging CI and local test execution times.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author reports local test runner wall time dropped from 110.8s to 96.4s (-13%) and accumulated runtime dropped from 1715s to 1369s (-20%) on an 18-thread x86-64 machine (PR description).",
    "Author CI runs showed test_runner.py runtime improvements across multiple environments: macOS native (-9%), 32-bit ARM (-11%), Windows native (-14%), and previous releases job (-15%) (PR description)."
